# Judge item J1697

Does the finding describe the labelled defect? `describes`, `partially`, or `does-not-describe`.

## Finding

``` text
head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/resources/config.ts:182 — `isAgyRouted` gates a google voice only under `cli-only`, but `prefer-cli` is documented (.loa.config.yaml.example:728) as "CLI first, HTTP last": cheval dispatches the gemini-headless hop first, the new refusal is a ConfigError that hard-aborts the chain, so Bridgebuilder plans the google voice and cheval fails it — the DEGRADED outcome FR-1 claims to remove. Gate `prefer-cli` as agy-routed too (or make the refusal walkable).
head/.claude/scripts/flatline-orchestrator.sh:534 — same gap in the Flatline planner: `_tertiary_routes_to_agy` returns 1 for `prefer-cli`, so a Google tertiary under prefer-cli is planned, dispatched, and refused by cheval with INVALID_CONFIG instead of running 2-model mode as `disabled_by_opt_in`.
head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py:2544 — `AgyOptInRequiredError` is caught by the generic `ChevalError` arm (and by the top-level `ConfigError` handlers) which emit `_error_json(code, message, retryable)` without `context`, so `failure_class: opt_in_required` never reaches the stderr JSON; the arm also aborts the whole invocation instead of walking, so an HTTP hop with a valid key placed after the agy hop is never tried.
head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/types.py:507 — the docstring says `failure_class` is "the machine-readable seam planners read as not planned"; nothing serializes it (see cheval.py:2544) and every planner in this PR reads the YAML key with yq instead. Either pass `**e.context`  …
```

