# Judge item J1720

Does the finding describe the labelled defect? `describes`, `partially`, or `does-not-describe`.

## Finding

``` text
head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/endpoint_policy.py:156 — HIGH: `validate_providers` admits `allow_insecure_endpoint` / `dispatch_group: local` for every non-CLI provider type, but only `OpenAIAdapter` (`providers/openai_adapter.py:217-223`) builds and passes the `TransportPolicy`; an opted-in `type: anthropic`/`google` provider loads and then runs on the default transport (`providers/base.py:304`, `:332`): plain http through the proxy env, urllib redirects followed — contradicting the module docstring and `.loa.config.yaml.example:1229-1232`. Refuse the opt-in for unsupported adapter types at load or plumb `policy=` into every adapter.
head/.claude/loa/reference/scripts-reference.md:73 — HIGH: documents "refuses a hosted probe under `local_voices`" (also `README.md:30`, `.loa.config.yaml.example:818`, `multi-model-reference.md:102`), but `model-health-probe.sh` (`:1428-1546`, `:1756`) never reads `hounfour.locality`; under `local_voices` the probe still sends API keys to the three hosted vendors. Implement the gate (hop-locality.py + the dissent's refusal line) or remove the probe from all four sentences.
head/.loa.config.yaml.example:1624 — MEDIUM: the `budget_cents` comment (also `:1690`) still says the gate prices ONE call and does not count the companion, while `adversarial-review.sh:4329-4335` now sums primary + companion first hop + every advisory voice; a budget tuned for one voice may now exit 4. Rewrite the comments (and ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW.md "per-voice cap") …
```

